# requirements/data-sources/curation.ears
capability: Curation and storage
owner: data-sources
requirements:
  - id: DSI-005
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The curation service shall record dialect id, dialect version and the raw parent artifact id on every curated dataset."
    rationale: "Curated data must cite the raw bytes and mapping they came from."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.contract.test_kernel_fakes.TestDatasetRepository::test_curated_children_cite_their_raw_parent"
      - "python/tests.unit.kernel.test_domain_values::test_curated_artifacts_cite_dialect_and_parent"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_acquire_dataset::test_acquisition_records_query_release_licence_citation_checksum_size_and_time"
  - id: DSI-006
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If a source descriptor declares no licence, then the system shall block curation of that source."
    rationale: "Data without a licence cannot be redistributed in a bundle."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.unit.kernel.test_domain_values::test_source_without_licence_cannot_be_curated"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_acquire_dataset::test_missing_licence_blocks_curation"
  - id: DSI-010
    pattern: state
    text: "While NAS free space is below the configured threshold, the system shall refuse new acquisitions."
    rationale: "NAS exhaustion fails workflows; refuse early instead."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T5]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_acquire_dataset::test_low_free_space_refuses_new_acquisitions"
  - id: DSI-020
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The curation service shall map every source magnitude that a registered test reads into its canonical column."
    rationale: "photometric-corroboration reads j_mag and k_mag, but the 2MASS dialect kept them only in quality_flags under the archive's names, so on Praesepe the test examined no star although 3,907 of 4,099 had a 2MASS row (#141). The 2MASS dialect 1.1.0 maps J, H and Ks into canonical columns (canonical-astrometry 1.1.0, additive), and a test runs photometric-corroboration on rows the packaged dialect curated. Rows acquired before a dialect change are curated again with the dialect in force (the raw download is reused), so a rerun sees the new columns."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_photometry_dialect::test_the_2mass_dialect_puts_j_h_and_k_in_canonical_columns"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_photometry_dialect::test_photometric_corroboration_examines_dialect_curated_2mass_rows"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_acquire_dataset::test_rows_curated_with_an_earlier_dialect_are_curated_again_and_never_fetched_again"
